f=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bx-vPsIPfm_keWlYNld1cmo5SEE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> they <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bx-vPsIPfm_kY3o0RkpBZTBUeUk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">are</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 01-12-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T21:36:08-08:00","id":7862,"title":"","content":"I started yet again ANOTHER project. I think I have 7 or 8 models in progress now. most of them are at the painting stage. the only reason I havve so many stuck at painting is that I have to paint in my garage because that's the only place well ventilated enough for me to spray my airbrush. I don't have a proper spray booth or anything (I took a giant cardboard box I got from an order of model kits, cut a a giant square hole in the back and put an AC filter in it.) the Air brush makes everything look so nice its just that once I start painting I'm going to be painting for weeks because I dislike doing it until I'm in the mood to do it. The project I just started is this guy: <a href=\"http://www.hlj.com/product/CYVCH6361/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hlj.com/product/CYVCH6361/</a> its pretty fucking awesome because its so strange looking to me. Basically they took an m4 armored half-track truck, got rid of all the seats for GIs, filled it with mortar shells and put the 81mm mortar in the back. Its not a large artillery piece but the 81mm mortar is actually a full 6cm larger than the shell used by the Sherman medium tank. the difference is, this was mostly 